    <!-- Unit Overview -->
    <section class="welcome-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-compass section-icon"></i> Unit Overview</h2>
        <p>The transition from abstract algorithms to executable code. This unit focuses on the automation of logic through programming constructs. It introduces the concept of state (variables), transformation (operators), and robustness (exception handling).</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Syllabus Links -->
    <section class="content-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-bookmark section-icon"></i> What You'll Learn</h2>
        <div class="learning-points">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>B2.1.1</strong> — Global and local variables, declaration, initialization, and primitive data types (int, float, double, char, Boolean).
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>B2.1.2</strong> — String manipulation, concatenation, and substring extraction (slicing in Python).
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>B2.1.3</strong> — Exception handling (try/except/finally) to manage unexpected inputs or resource unavailability.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>B2.1.4</strong> — Debugging techniques including trace tables, breakpoints, and print statements.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

